<title>SINGAPORE: Parkway 1996 net profit up 109 pct.</title>
<headline>Parkway 1996 net profit up 109 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   48.02 vs   23.02</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)	  6.00 vs     nil</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	16.00 vs    8.04</p>
<p>    Grp share fully diluted  14.15 vs    7.54</p>
<p>    Turnover		    389.57 vs  284.74</p>
<p>    Investment income	   1.30 vs    1.28</p>
<p>    Income incl. interest    19.22 vs   15.66</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)	 47.98 vs   37.84</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 26.95 vs   18.13</p>
<p>    Profits from associates  17.24 vs   13.76</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     69.68 vs   37.62</p>
<p>    Tax			    21.06 vs   14.43</p>
<p>    Minority interests (loss) 0.60 vs    0.17</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries    (gain) 2.16 vs   93.70 (loss)</p>
<p>    Dividend payment date     June 20, 1997</p>
<p>    Books closing date	  June 10, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Parkway Holdings Ltd is a property and health care company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 870 3199)</p>
</text>
